#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/02-tech-stack.md:214
#: 5c307ea5ab424bf4971330206233a462
msgid ""
"**Stack thread.** `nua_create`, `nua_invite`, `nua_respond`, "
"`nua_destroy`, and the NUA callback all run on the thread that drives "
"`su_root_run` / `su_root_step`. Do not hunt dialplan, block on SQL, or "
"sleep in the callback — that stalls SIP I/O. FreeSWITCH copies the event "
"with `nua_save_event` onto `signal_data_queue` or `msg_queue`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/02-tech-stack.md:215
#: b956e0f8a90a421bbf024a3af748f8a8
msgid ""
"**Handle lifetime.** One `nua_handle_t` per dialog. Inbound handles are "
"created by the stack; bind application state with `nua_handle_bind`. "
"Destroy with `nua_handle_destroy`. Crossing threads requires "
"`nua_handle_ref` / `nua_handle_unref` (and the `*_user` variants)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/1.architecture/02-tech-stack.md:216
#: b22614b742ee4d5fa25df6848e778cc3
msgid ""
"**Memory.** `sip_t` is valid only until the callback returns. Copy Call-"
"ID / Contact into a `su_home_t` (`su_strdup`) or your own heap. "
"Destroying the home frees those copies."
msgstr ""

